  "note": "A watcher install with a unique canary in every place W-BETA B.3 names. The report is built from it, unpacked, and every canary (and the expanded $HOME, and each $SECRET{} value of the shared corpus) must have 0 hits in the zip. Canaries sit in the allowlisted streams (in fields the export must drop or hash), in the never-opened files (jobs.jsonl, evidence-index.tsv, queue-adds.jsonl, paths.jsonl), in the summary copy and the handoff, in the settings file and in the git remote. The account and host canaries need the process to see them: the case sets USER and LOGNAME, and the host canary comes from a `hostname` PATH stub (B.3 reads `hostname -s`), with STORE_TEST_HOSTNAME as the fallback for a helper that reads the host name another way (needs/fix-to-watch.md). The bucket is a topic bucket, so the ticket names no folder: `expect.identity_list` is the B.3 list for this install, and the `transform_only` canaries contain no identity string, so 0 hits for them proves the export transform, not the identity scan.",
  "clock": "the case sets now to 2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00 (ids.json)",
